@* MainLayout — scaffolded exactly once from the model (OverwriteDisabled), same as
   MainLayoutHeader/Sider/Footer/Profile. After that first generation, this file's region
   composition is this skill's job to keep in sync, same as it keeps Header/Sider/Footer/Profile
   markup in sync — but the ownership here is much narrower: only WHICH region components are
   referenced, nothing else.

   - <MainLayoutHeader /> and <MainLayoutSider /> are core — always present. Never remove them.
   - <MainLayoutFooter /> is conditional: present only when MainLayoutFooter.razor exists for
     this Layout (a Footer was modeled). If that file exists but the reference below is missing,
     add it as the last sibling inside the layout wrapper, as shown here. If the file no longer
     exists (Footer removed from the model) but the reference remains, remove it.
   - Never add or remove <MainLayoutProfile /> here — that reference lives only inside
     MainLayoutHeader.razor (see app-header-auth-sample.razor), never in MainLayout.razor itself.
   - Everything else in this file — the outer wrapper element(s), its CSS classes, and where
     @Body sits inside that wrapper — was decided by the first scaffold generation and is NOT
     this skill's concern. Preserve it exactly, whatever shape it happens to be in a given
     project (it may differ from the shape below). Do not rewrite, reorder, or "clean up" any
     of it. *@

<div class="ux-app-shell">
    <MainLayoutHeader />
    <MainLayoutSider />
    <main class="ux-app-content">@Body</main>
    <MainLayoutFooter />
</div>
